.TH PING 1
.SH NAME
ping \- send IPv4 ICMP echo requests
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ping
.RI [ -c " COUNT] ADDRESS"
.SH DESCRIPTION
Send echo requests to an IPv4 address or hostname and report replies, TTL and
round-trip time. Four requests are sent by default. Count must be positive.
Root access is required to open the raw ICMP socket. Ctrl-C stops the command.
.PP
Timing is based on the guest host-clock timer, with 100 ms display resolution.
The Ethernet interface must have an attached peer and a suitable address,
mask and gateway. For the default host-only link try ping -c 3 192.168.64.1.
.SH SEE ALSO
ifconfig(1)
